    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}\u2061A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\u2220A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\frac{20}{3}\\text{\u00a0cm} \\\\ b & =AC \\\\ m\u2220A & ={135}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{135}^{\u2218}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ \\frac{35\\sqrt{2}}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot \\frac{20}{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{135}^{\u2218} \\\\ \\frac{35\\sqrt{2}}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot \\frac{20}{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{35\\sqrt{2}}{4} & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{3}b \\\\ b & =\\frac{\\frac{35\\sqrt{2}}{4}}{\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{3}} \\\\ b & =\\frac{21}{4}\\text{\u00a0cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=\\frac{21}{4}\\,\\text{cm}.$"
  },
